      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T00:45:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was hoping that these Rust-side pieces can also move to `rust/common` (in addition to `impl ... Read`).\n\n* `rust/common/BUILD.bazel` would define a new `rust_static_library`\n  (let\u0027s maybe focus on Bazel builds / `bazelisk build` first and worry\n  about gn/ninja builds later)\n* The new `rust/common` Rust library would:\n    - Have `#[cxx::bridge]` with\n        - `type StreamAdapter;`\n        - `read`, `seek_from_start`, etc.\n    - Have `impl ... Read for StreamAdapter`\n    - Re-export public API with something like: `pub use StreamAdapter \u003d ffi::StreamAdapter`.\n* The old `rust/png/FFI.rs` would:\n    - Replace `type StreamAdapter` with `type StreamAdapter \u003d other_crate_name::StreamAdapter` based on https://cxx.rs/extern-c++.html#safely-unifying-occurrences-of-an-extern-type-across-bridges\n    - Delete declarationf of `fn read`, `fn seek_from_start`, etc.\n\nBasing `rust/common/io_traits_ffi.rs` around a macro seems to introduce extra complexity - I don\u0027t understand why this is needed.\n\n--------------------------\n\nI understand that covering GN/ninja build is a bit difficult.  So I think getting the Bazel build working first and getting that reviewed may be a reasonable way forward.\n\nThe GN/ninja difficulties mostly arise from the fact that definitions of build targets are spread across the Skia repo and the Chromium repo (and now the PDFium repo) and both/all repos have to keep working in intermediate states.  So if we stick with the current Skia approach of providing `skia/gn/*.gni` files and having Chromium/PDFium/etc assemble `BUILD.gn` files out of these `.gni` files, then I think we would have to do a multi-step CL dance similar to:\n\n* Skia: Land new `//rust/common` Rust crate\n  (new crate builds via Bazelisk + `.gni` files cover new `.rs` sources).\n  No changes to old PNG targets yet.\n* Chromium/PDFium: Start using the new `.rs` sources.\n  (Tweaking their `//skia/BUILD.gn` to define a new `rust_static_library` target + make the old PNG/FFI Rust crate depend on the new target.)\n* Skia: Actually start using the new crate from the old PNG crate\n  (in Bazel + GN/ninja builds)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "49f2f49df4769e7dbb78ae2208d1534efc4bd087",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08908075_9828d91d",
