      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T16:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason why I had to keep function definition in rust/png/FFI.rs was an error that I was getting when building, because SkStreamAdapter did not satisfied the UniquePtrTarget trait.\n\nerror[E0277]: the trait bound `SkStreamAdapter: UniquePtrTarget` is not satisfied\n  --\u003e rust/common/io_traits_ffi.rs:79:31\n   |\n79 | fn force_unique_ptr_bridge(_: cxx::UniquePtr\u003cSkStreamAdapter\u003e) {\n   |                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the trait `UniquePtrTarget` is not implemented for `SkStreamAdapter`\n   |\n   \u003d help: the following other types implement trait `UniquePtrTarget`:\n             CxxString\n             CxxVector\u003cT\u003e\nnote: required by a bound in `UniquePtr`\n  --\u003e external/rules_rust++crate+crates__cxx-1.0.168/src/unique_ptr.rs:23:1\n\nAfter some investigation I found that this should be generated by cxx bridge, but it is only used if the types is actually used in any function of the bridge. The workaround I have found now and which allows to remove the function definition from rust/png/FFI.rs is to define some dummy function in io_traits_ffi.rs which makes use to it, so that cxx bridge generates the expected trait. Do you know if there is any other way that we can force the generation?",
